 "interpretation": "The song conveys a deep experience of the devotee's spiritual longing (viraha). The sudden mystical visit of the Beloved leaves the soul in awe: the touch was so fleeting that the devotee did not have time to express the overflowing emotions. Ragas Diipak (the raga of fire and passion) and Megh Mallar (the raga of rain, refreshing coolness, and union) symbolize the polarities of the spiritual path: the burning thirst of separation and the saving downpour of divine grace. Although physically or mentally it seems that boundless expanses (\"hundreds of yojanas\") lie between the soul and Supreme Consciousness, the inner space of the mind remains unconditionally inundated with His subtle presence.",
